---
apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
metadata:
  name: {{ code_server_k8s_workspace_claim }}
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
spec:
  # The ONLY code-server data that is backed up. code-server-config (10 Gi, class `longhorn`)
  # carries ~6.7 G of derived state — 5.8 G of orphaned extension installs under
  # .local/share/code-server/extensions, 637 M of live extensions, 223 M of caches — against
  # ~2.5 M of things nobody can regenerate. Backing up the whole volume made ONE service 52% of
  # the 13.72 GiB backup set and 3,668 of its 7,023 blocks, which at one Class-B GET per block
  # put a code-server restore at 147% of B2's 2,500/day allowance: not restorable in a day.
  #
  # A plain claim, not a seeded one: the initContainer in deployment.yaml.j2 migrates the four
  # paths off the config volume on first boot. Nothing is deleted there — the config PVC keeps
  # its copy, it simply stops being backed up.
  #
  # `longhorn` (backed up), unlike the config volume which moved to
  # k3s_longhorn_nobackup_volumes. storageClassName is immutable, which is why the already-bound
  # config volume needs that list rather than a class change.
  accessModes:
    - ReadWriteOnce
  storageClassName: {{ code_server_k8s_workspace_storage_class }}
  resources:
    requests:
      storage: {{ code_server_k8s_workspace_size }}
